Simplify: assert (0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size())) => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < index; (this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i)) || (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null));

But equality of references covers null equality as well: (this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i))) works for null and same reference. However for objects that may be equal but not same reference, spec might want equals. In earlier examples they used .equals for query. Use .equals with null handling: (this.get(i) == null ? \old(this.get(i)) == null : this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i)))).

Thus final assert:

assert (0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size())) => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < index; (this.get(i) == null ? \old(this.get(i)) == null : this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i))));

